1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Demo using actual Knot Studio results, a recreated interface, and shortened timings.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Load a blackboard photograph and recognize the link automatically.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,500
Recognize drawing converts the picture into an editable diagram.

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:13,000
Five components, eight crossings. Needs review: inspect the crossings inferred from chalk.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Load an iPad drawing and recognize its strands and crossings.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,500
Recognize drawing converts the picture into an editable diagram.

7
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:21,000
The iPad sketch becomes a knot with six crossings and one component.

8
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Load a figure from a research paper. Review the marked labels before recognizing.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Remove the four marked numeric labels while preserving the strands.

10
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,500
Recognize drawing converts the picture into an editable diagram.

11
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:32,000
The cleaned paper figure becomes an editable four-crossing knot.

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,500
Start a new sketch. We will use this one figure-eight for every operation that follows.

13
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:47,500
Draw one closed strand. Hold Shift at an undercrossing; the other strokes pass over.

14
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,500
Recognize the hand-drawn figure-eight to start editing.

15
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:53,000
Four crossings, one component. Keep this view fixed throughout the editing session.

16
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Hold Shift and pull a strand underneath its neighbors to add crossing pairs: 4 → 8 crossings.

17
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,500
Watch the small triangle on the right. Slide the selected strand to the left; keep the view fixed.

18
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:15,500
Continue on the same figure-eight. Slide a strand past a crossing; the crossing count stays unchanged.

19
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:18,000
Choose Add curl… and select the sign of the new crossing.

20
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Choose a positive curl, then place it on the strand.

21
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Click a strand point, then the side where the curl should appear.

22
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,500
The new curl adds one crossing while preserving the knot type.

23
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:28,500
Choose Add curl… again to add a second curl.

24
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:31,000
Choose a negative curl, then place it on the strand.

25
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Choose a strand point and a side for this second curl.

26
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,500
The new curl adds one crossing while preserving the knot type.

27
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:39,500
Simplification 1: click the green curl. Crossings: 10 → 9.

28
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:41,500
The same figure-eight remains. Each click is a separate simplification and undo step.

29
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:44,500
Simplification 2: click the green curl. Crossings: 9 → 8.

30
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:46,500
The same figure-eight remains. Each click is a separate simplification and undo step.

31
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,500
Simplification 3: click the purple bigon. Crossings: 8 → 6.

32
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:51,500
The same figure-eight remains. Each click is a separate simplification and undo step.

33
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:54,000
Choose Minimize energy… and circle the rough part of this diagram.

34
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,500
Enclose the bends to smooth. The strands outside the selected region stay fixed.

35
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:07,500
The selected rough region relaxes. Exterior strands stay fixed and the PD code is preserved.

36
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:10,000
Stop keeps the improved layout. Undo restores the diagram from before the run.

37
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Enable Full screen region, then minimize the whole visible figure-eight in the same fixed view.

38
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Continue from the local result. The whole visible diagram relaxes with the same PD code.

39
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,500
Stop keeps the improved layout. Undo restores the diagram from before the run.

40
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:29,000
Keep the final diagram on screen and scroll down to its code tabs.

41
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:34,000
The PD code belongs to this final figure-eight. Hover over the code box to copy it.

42
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Switch to TikZ code. This same diagram exports with the smooth curves shown on the canvas.

43
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,500
Use Save… → TikZ code to export this figure as a .tex file.

44
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:47,500
Draw, recognize, and manipulate your knot diagram.
